# Trivy Ignore File for Audio Processor
# This file documents vulnerabilities that are accepted risks or cannot be fixed yet.
# Each entry should have a clear justification.

# CVE-2025-13601 - libglib2.0-0t64 heap buffer overflow in g_escape_uri_string()
# Status: No fix available in Debian as of 2025-12-06
# Severity: HIGH
# Risk Assessment: LOW for this application
# Justification:
#   - Vulnerability requires calling g_escape_uri_string() with a very large number
#     of unacceptable characters that need escaping
#   - This application does not use GLib URI escaping functionality
#   - Upstream patches exist (glib 2.86.2) but not yet backported to Debian
#   - Tracking: Debian bug #1121488
# References:
#   - https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2025-13601
#   - https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/glib/-/issues/3827
#   - https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/glib/-/merge_requests/4914
# Review Date: 2025-12-06
# Next Review: When Debian releases patch (monitor bug #1121488)
CVE-2025-13601
